{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533118-ideia-about-masquerade-and-requiem","id":1533118,"title":"Ideia about Masquerade and Requiem.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-25T05:16:31-07:00","id":1533118,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon7.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Ideia about Masquerade and Requiem.","content":"This is a crazy idea I had to try to fit in a cross-over between Requiem and Masquerade, not that there has any reason. It's quite simple actually, first we have the original story of VTM, Cain was cursed, created the first city, second generation, third generation, betrayal, curse, Jyhad, Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchy and you know how it goes. So how do you fit in Requiem's kindred? My idea would be the following, taking advantage of the contagion events, I would say that the vampires of Requiem were born from an infection of the older Cainites, which, then, the antediluvians and fourth and fifth generation Methuselahs are missing, for the most part, not because they were hidden, but because they were transformed, in general they even forgot that they were once Cainites, a bit forced, but I think it works, and I know that it leaves some holes and there's a lot left to explain, but that's the part I wanted some ideas, what do you think? How do you think the world would function with this change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T11:47:27-07:00","id":1533128,"title":"","content":"For me, one of the features that makes VtR vampires interesting is that they have multiple origins, explained in multiple myths. That\u2019s lost or at least debunked if they become Cainites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T13:15:14-07:00","id":1533132,"title":"","content":"One thing I have as a secret in my chronicles is that some of the Bloodlines in the setting are not descended directly from Caine. Instead, they were independently created post-Deluge. They ultimately have the same origin in the sense is that they were all similarly cursed and made infernal pacts with the &quot;Dark Mother&quot; (Lilith) - which is how Caine actually gained his powers in my chronicle. But they are not his direct descendant like the 13 Clans are. Of course, being creations post-Flood and for less mythologically important crimes, the first member/founder of those bloodlines aren't anywhere close in power to Caine, and are effectively only sixth or seventh generation (as if they were of Caine's line) even though they are technically the first generation of their bloodline.<br /> <br /> I obviously don't use that origin for any &quot;bloodlines&quot; that are just obvious sub-lineages of existing clans (Ahrimanes, the various Cappadocian lineages, Danava, Kiasyd, Salubri, City Gangrel, etc.) or are actually just small &quot;sects&quot; or societies that people and the game incorrectly refer to as &quot;bloodlines&quot; like the Children of Osiris or Baali. But that secret origin <i>might</i> apply to more mysterious bloodlines like the Daughters of Cacophony, Lhiannon, Nagaraja, or Bonsam.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to bring in one of the unique VtR clans into my setting, I'd either just make them one of the real clans descended from Caine (if I wanted them to be an important part of the setting and distinct from the other clans), make them a sub-lineage of an existing clan (and align their in-clan disciplines/weaknesses appropriately but keep their flavor text), or make them one of the bloodlines with an actual separate creation (if I wanted them to be a minor part of the setting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T14:16:07-07:00","id":1533136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533118-ideia-about-masquerade-and-requiem?p=1533132#post1533132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I have as a secret in my chronicles is that some of the Bloodlines in the setting are not descended directly from Caine. Instead, they were independently created post-Deluge. They ultimately have the same origin in the sense is that they were all similarly cursed and made infernal pacts with the &quot;Dark Mother&quot; (Lilith) - which is how Caine actually gained his powers in my chronicle. But they are not his direct descendant like the 13 Clans are. Of course, being creations post-Flood and for less mythologically important crimes, the first member/founder of those bloodlines aren't anywhere close in power to Caine, and are effectively only sixth or seventh generation (as if they were of Caine's line) even though they are technically the first generation of their bloodline.<br /> <br /> I obviously don't use that origin for any &quot;bloodlines&quot; that are just obvious sub-lineages of existing clans (Ahrimanes, the various Cappadocian lineages, Danava, Kiasyd, Salubri, City Gangrel, etc.) or are actually just small &quot;sects&quot; or societies that people and the game incorrectly refer to as &quot;bloodlines&quot; like the Children of Osiris or Baali. But that secret origin <i>might</i> apply to more mysterious bloodlines like the Daughters of Cacophony, Lhiannon, Nagaraja, or Bonsam.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to bring in one of the unique VtR clans into my setting, I'd either just make them one of the real clans descended from Caine (if I wanted them to be an important part of the setting and distinct from the other clans), make them a sub-lineage of an existing clan (and align their in-clan disciplines/weaknesses appropriately but keep their flavor text), or make them one of the bloodlines with an actual separate creation (if I wanted them to be a minor part of the setting).</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly could give more work, but make more sense and give some openings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T03:13:30-07:00","id":1533801,"title":"","content":"I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28047-lewisdavis","name":"LewisDavis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}